    "title": "Ralph and Elizabeth Pyszkowski: Greater Things Are Yet to Come",
    "text": "The great John the Baptist sat alone in a dark, dingy cell. It appeared that all his efforts had been in vain. Surrounded by iron bars and gloomy scenery, he was discouraged. He even asked if Jesus was the messiah or if they should be looking for someone else (Luke 7:19)? Jesus sent word back to him and said, “The blind see, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, to the poor the gospel is preached.” Little did John know, heaven had come to earth and indescribable miracles were happening outside of his prison. In spite of our situations, the Lord has the bigger picture and greater plans yet to come.\nIf someone like John the Baptist can get discouraged, it can happen to anyone. At times, our vision can be clouded by the circumstances all around us. We may not be able to perceive what God is doing or grasp a positive outcome. It is important to trust the Lord as he knows all things. Sometimes he moves in ways that we can’t see. Instead of focusing on the gloomy picture around us, we have got to keep our eyes on Jesus and his word. He cannot lie and all of his promises are true. We should meditate on them and allow them to build our faith. We can trust the Lord for the best outcomes even in the direst situations.",
